  "caseId": "case13",
  "description": "Two things at once, and they belong together. First the seeding deviation: there is no usrsec fixture in app/data/ASCII, so this dataset is seeded inline from app/jcl/DUSRSECJ.jcl:L35-L44, whose IEBGENER stream carries rows of FIFTY-SEVEN characters while app/cpy/CSUSR01Y.cpy declares EIGHTY. The missing span is SEC-USR-FILLER X(23), and the pad is declared once through the USRSEC_FILLER_PAD_57_TO_80 normalisation and applied at SEED time by the harness - never at comparison time - which is why every row of this expectation is written out at the copybook's eighty. Second the arm: the write is refused with outcome OTHER and no RESP declared at all, which is the permanent-error shape. The controller records it as 'no RESP reported' rather than as any of the three values :250-274 names, so it cannot be mistaken for NORMAL, DUPKEY or DUPREC, and it lands on WHEN OTHER with 'Unable to Add User...'. Ten rows, unchanged, each eighty bytes wide.",
